       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 600 mg daily is three times the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day. At that dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and severe GI or bleeding effects. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nIt may be a typo. Common sertraline doses are:\n- **Depression, anxiety, PTSD:** start at 25\u201350 mg daily, then titrate. The usual range is 50\u2013200 mg.\n- **Possible intended dose:** 50 mg, 60 mg, or 100 mg.\n\nCould you tell me the dose you meant? If you really do want 600 mg, for example as part of a specific plan, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
